### Test HTTP requests for Coduflow Task API
### Server runs on http://localhost:8080

### 1. Create a new task
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/task
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Implement user authentication",
  "status": "TODO",
  "priority": 1,
  "estimated_time": 120,
  "logged_time": 0,
  "due_date": "2024-12-31T23:59:59Z"
}

### 2. Create another task with minimal fields
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/task
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Write API documentation",
  "status": "TODO"
}

### 3. Create task with DOING status
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/task
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Fix login bug",
  "status": "DOING",
  "priority": 2,
  "estimated_time": 60,
  "logged_time": 30
}

### 4. Create task with COMPLETE status
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/task
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Setup CI/CD pipeline",
  "status": "COMPLETE",
  "priority": 3,
  "estimated_time": 180,
  "logged_time": 200
}

### 5. Update task status (replace :id with actual task ID from response)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/task/69d49d2d79471fc338e87de9/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "DOING"
}

### 6. Update task status to COMPLETE
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/task/69d49d2d79471fc338e87de9/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "COMPLETE"
}

### 7. Delete a task (replace :id with actual task ID from response)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/v1/task/:id

### 8. Test validation error - missing required field
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/task
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "TODO"
}

### 9. Test validation error - invalid status
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/task
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Invalid task",
  "status": "INVALID_STATUS"
}

### 10. Test validation error - invalid priority
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/task
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Task with invalid priority",
  "status": "TODO",
  "priority": 10
}

### 11. Test validation error - negative estimated time
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/task
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Task with negative time",
  "status": "TODO",
  "estimated_time": -10
}

### 12. Update status with invalid ID format
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/task/invalid-id/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "DOING"
}

### 13. Delete with invalid ID format
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/v1/task/invalid-id

### 14. Update status of non-existent task (use valid ObjectID format)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/task/507f1f77bcf86cd799439011/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "DOING"
}

### 15. Delete non-existent task (use valid ObjectID format)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/v1/task/507f1f77bcf86cd799439011

### 16. Test with optional fields omitted
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/task
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Task with only required fields",
  "status": "TODO",
  "priority": null,
  "estimated_time": null,
  "logged_time": null,
  "due_date": null
}

### 17. Test with future due date
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/task
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Task with future deadline",
  "status": "TODO",
  "due_date": "2025-06-30T18:00:00Z"
}

### 18. Test with past due date
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/task
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Overdue task",
  "status": "TODO",
  "due_date": "2023-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}

### 19. Test with zero time values
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/task
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Task with zero time",
  "status": "TODO",
  "estimated_time": 0,
  "logged_time": 0
}

### 20. Test with large time values
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/task
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Long running task",
  "status": "TODO",
  "estimated_time": 9999,
  "logged_time": 5000
}